# Three frames deep. The arrow of `maker` lies in the frame of `maker`. The arrow of `middle` holds it and lies in the frame of `middle`: `keepLater` only calls what arrives. The arrow of `keepLater` is pushed to a list, so it is made in the heap, and what it captures is moved: the arrow of `middle`, and with it the arrow of `maker`, which no code of `keepLater` names.
# f1 = keepLater, f2 = middle, f4 = maker, f3 = deep
